cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, pipeline, or processed dataset in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Spatiotemporal Data Analytics and Dimensionality Reduction for Social Vulnerability Assessment in Region XI (2020–2024)"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible spatial data science pipeline for constructing a longitudinally comparable,
  scale-normalized Social Vulnerability Index (SoVI) across Region XI (Davao Region), Philippines
  from 2020 to 2024 (N = 30 province-year observations). Integrating 15 multi-source Philippine
  Statistics Authority (PSA) indicators via pooled multi-year Z-score standardization and
  Varimax-rotated Principal Component Analysis (PCA), the framework eliminates baseline drift,
  tracks longitudinal risk trajectories, and validates stability through Leave-One-Year-Out (LOYO)
  cross-validation, Global Moran's I spatial diagnostics, Eckart-Young-Mirsky subspace optimality
  bounds, and a 10,000-run Monte Carlo simulation.
